--TEST--
An `[app.limits.hard]` ceiling below the global `[limits]` start the block inherits stops the run with E0601 — `rule:config/ceilings-are-their-own-directives`
--FILE nvs.toml--
[limits]
memory = "1G"

[[app]]
root = "."

[app.limits.hard]
memory = "512M"
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The block lowers the ceiling and keeps the global start of 1G, so the run is refused.
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0601]: `[limits] memory` is `1G`, which is above its ceiling of `512M`
%A
